```rust
fn render_tweet(text: &str, entities: Vec<Entity>) -> String {
    let mut rendered = String::from(text);
    for entity in entities {
        let start = entity.start;
        let end = entity.end;
        let replacement = entity.replacement;
        rendered.replace_range(start..end, replacement);
    }
    rendered
}

struct Entity {
    replacement: String,
    start: usize,  
    end: usize,  
}
```

We define an Entity struct to represent each entity with its replacement text, start index and end index.

The render_tweet function takes the original text and a vector of Entity structs. 
It starts with the original text and then iterates through each entity. 
It replaces the substring from start to end index with the replacement text using replace_range().

Example usage:
```rust
let text = "Hello #rustlang!";

let entities = vec![
    Entity {
        replacement: "#rust",
        start: 7,
        end: 16  
    }
];

let rendered = render_tweet(text, entities);

assert_eq!(rendered, "Hello #rust!");
```']

